O:12195","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-1. E s ta b lis h m e n t,\n1-101. There is established the President’s Commission on United States-  \nLiberian Relations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-1","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The membership of the Commission shall be composed of not more  \nthan sixteen persons, as follows. Twelve shall be appointed by the President.  \nThe President of the United States Senate and the Speaker of the United  \nStates House of Representatives are each invited to designate two members.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-102(a)","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-102(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The President shall designate a Chairman from among the members of the  \nCommission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-102(b)","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-102(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-201. The Commission shall conduct a comprehensive review of our relations  \nwith Liberia and will provide recommendations to improve this relationship.  \nIn particular, the Commission shall:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-201 (lead-in)","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-201","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Make an overall assessm ent of United States-Liberian relations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-201(a)","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-201(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Identify problem areas and constraints to a better functioning relationship.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-201(b)","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-201(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Develop appropriate recommendations based on the Commission’s find­\nings.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-201(c)","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-201(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-202. The Commission shall prepare and transmit to the President of the  \nUnited States and to the Secretary of State, a final report of its findings and  \nrecommendations.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-202","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-202","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-301. Members of the Commission who are not otherwise full-time officers or  \nemployees of the Federal government shall receive no compensation for their  \nwork on the Commission. All members shall be entitled to travel expenses,  \nincluding per diem in lieu of subsistence, as authorized by law.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-301","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-301","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-302. The Department of State shall, to the extent permitted by law  and  \nsubject to the availability of funds, provide the Commission with such funds,  \nfacilities, support and services as may be necessary for the performance of the  \nCommission’s functions.\n\n=== PDF page 14 of 320 ===\n1 2374 Federal Register /  Vol. 45, No. 39 /  Tuesday, February 26, 1980 /  Presidential Documents\n1-4. F in a l R e p o r t a n d  T erm in a tio n\n1-401. The final report required by Section 1-202 of this Order shall be  \ntransmitted not later than two months from the date of the Commission’s visit  \nto Liberia.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-302","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-302","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1-402. The Commission shall terminate upon the transmittal of its final report,  \nbut in any event not later than six months from the date this Order is issued.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1-402","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:12195#sec1-402","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"45 FR 12373, PDF pages 13-14","sha256":"4a3a888f59911e68f8cad3e6b7b8dfab7f5089e179328599f852e965a22799db","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1980-02-26/pdf/FR-1980-02-26.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 11 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:12195"}
